 /*
- * Built-in iOS battery bring-up service. Default: 100%, AC, not charging.
- * negronibattery=1: read-only PM6150 polling every 30 seconds; voltage-derived
- * SOC is an UNCALIBRATED estimate, not a replacement for the Linux QG algo.
- * See report.md for binary evidence, register provenance and integration.
+ * NEGRONI (OnePlus 10 Pro 5G, SM8450): the battery as iOS reads it, an IOPMPowerSource.
+ *
+ * Why (patches/xnu/README-battery.md): the port's earlier class was the sweet
+ * (Redmi Note 10 Pro, PM6150) driver: PM6150 QG/SCHG addresses on SID 0 that do
+ * not exist on SM8450 (SID 0 is PMK8350; 0x1300 is its PON = the keys) and an
+ * arbiter v5 SPMI layer that rejects this v7 arbiter; slop patch 0089 then removed
+ * its personality, so iOS had no power source at all (status bar battery empty).
+ *
+ * On SM8450 the fuel gauge (an external gauge IC, `qcom,external_gauge`) and the
+ * charger are run by the ADSP charger PD and read over GLINK PMIC_RTR_ADSP_APPS;
+ * the HLOS devicetree has no gauge node. Until the ADSP runs (patch 0240 + a
+ * battmgr client), this service estimates the state of charge from what the
+ * application processor can measure:
+ *
+ * Default, READ ONLY (no PMIC write; observer-channel reads with a bounded poll, through the
+ * SPMI arbiter mapping that the RTC of patch 0203 also uses, bsd/dev/negroni_spmi.c):
+ *   PM8350B BCL, SID 3 0x4700 (live DT bcl@4700 "qcom,bcl-v5", qcom,pmic7-threshold;
+ *   downstream drivers/thermal/qcom/bcl_pmic5.c):
+ *     0x4746 MONITOR_EN   bit 7 = BCL monitor on (Linux sets it at probe; we only read it)
+ *     0x4772 VBAT_CONV_REQ non-zero = VBAT ADC on (Linux registers the vbat zone only then)
+ *     0x4776 VBAT_READ    u8, 49.827 mV per bit; 0x7f = no reading (which node it measures
+ *                         on the 2S pack is not known: above 5 V it is taken as the pack)
+ *     0x4786 IBAT_READ    s8, 78.127 mA per bit (default range factor), + = discharge
+ *                         (DT trips ibat-lvl0/1 9000/10000 mA are discharge limits)
+ * Opt-in negronibatt=4/5, VADC (writes the ADC7 conversion request registers only,
+ * 0x3140-0x3145/0x3147, when EE 0 owns that APID; Linux qcom-spmi-adc5.c adc7 path):
+ *   PMK8350 VADC SID 0 0x3100, channels of the live DT (vadc@3100):
+ *   0x38f pm8350b_vbat_sns   prescale 1/3      battery voltage (per-cell value, 2S pack)
+ *   0x311 pm8350b_usb_in_v_div_16  1/16        USBIN (VBUS): charger present
+ *   0x3a1 pm8350b_ichg_fb    1000/305185       charge current (uA)
+ *   0x317 pm8350b_iin_fb     32/100            input current (uA)
+ *   0x146 pm8350_hot_pocket_therm  ratiometric skin temperature (OPLUS skin_temp_chan)
+ *
+ * State of charge: open-circuit-voltage curve (4.45 V class cell, the DT's vfloat
+ * 4435 mV, power-off 3300 mV) with IR compensation, coulomb counting of the battery
+ * current (BCL IBAT both ways, or the VADC charge current), a slow pull toward the
+ * voltage value, monotonic smoothing (never up on battery, never down on a charger)
+ * and a slew limit. It is an ESTIMATE (CapacityEstimated = true).
+ *
+ * Boot-arg negronibatt:
+ *   0  no power source (the kernel before this patch)
+ *   1  read-only BCL estimate (default)
+ *   2  1 + diagnostics: a raw line per poll, a one-time PM8350B (SID 3) peripheral census,
+ *      and a line per change of a PM8350B peripheral's INT_RT_STS (plug-event discovery)
+ *   3  static 100 %, on AC, not charging (the old NegroniBattery fallback; no PMIC access)
+ *   4  1 + PMK8350 VADC conversions (better voltage, VBUS, charge current, skin temperature)
+ *   5  4 + the diagnostics of 2
+ * Keys follow AppleSmartBattery as the reference ports learned them (bergamota 0130,
+ * HackiOS RedwoodBattery.cpp): CurrentCapacity is the percentage with MaxCapacity 100;
+ * mAh go to AppleRaw*Capacity / NominalChargeCapacity / DesignCapacity. 20H392 powerd
+ * matches IOPMPowerSource and reads CurrentCapacity, MaxCapacity, AppleRawCurrentCapacity,
+ * AppleRawMaxCapacity, IsCharging, FullyCharged, ExternalConnected, ExternalChargeCapable,
+ * AppleRawExternalConnected, BatteryInstalled, Voltage, Amperage, InstantAmperage,
+ * Temperature, CycleCount, DesignCapacity, NominalChargeCapacity, TimeRemaining,
+ * AtCriticalLevel, AdapterDetails, BatteryData, PermanentFailureStatus (its strings).
+ * Log prefix "NEGRONI BATTERY:".
  */
